<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">South Peruvian Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1836 CE – 1839 CE · capital Tacna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The southern Peruvian state created by Andrés de Santa Cruz in 1836 as one of three members of the Peru-Bolivian Confederation.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz">Andrés de Santa Cruz's</a> Bolivian army defeated his Peruvian opponents, an assembly of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">departments</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arequipa">Arequipa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puno-region">Puno</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayacucho">Ayacucho</a>, met at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicuani">Sicuani</a> in March 1836 and declared the South Peruvian Republic. It was designed to join the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia">Republic of Bolivia</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-peruvian-republic">North Peruvian Republic</a> in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/peru-bolivian-confederation">Peru-Bolivian Confederation</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz">Santa Cruz</a> held effective power, with local presidents, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-herrera">Ramón Herrera</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-pio-de-tristan">Juan Pío de Tristán</a>, governing under his supervision. The southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/andecavi">Andes</a> had close economic links with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia">Bolivia</a>, and many in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arequipa">Arequipa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> favoured the union. The state adopted Santa Cruz's legal codes and sent delegates to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-tacna">Congress of Tacna</a> in 1837.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Chilean and Peruvian exile victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-yungay">Yungay</a> in January 1839, the confederation collapsed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agustin-gamarra">Agustín Gamarra</a> reunited the south with the rest of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-peru">Republic of Peru</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz">Santa Cruz</a>'s project of joining southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia">Bolivia</a> was never revived.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/south-peruvian-republic.jpg" alt="South Peruvian Republic" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_Peru.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1836 CE – 1839 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tacna</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ramón Herrera, Juan Pío de Tristán</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish, Quechua, Aymara</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/peru">Peru</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of South Peru, Estado Sud-Peruano</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1838&amp;focus=south-peruvian-republic" aria-label="South Peruvian Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2775 2847 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where South Peruvian Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3095 3103L3095 3103M3095 3103L2883 2883"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3095 3103h0M2883 2883h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3095 3103h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3095 3103h0"/></svg></a><figcap